  "title": "Qt: Avoid using QTextCodec in simple_dialog",
  "description": "QTextCodec is part of the Qt5 Core Compat module, so reduce usage\nof it.\n\nQString::fromLocal8Bit() is available in both Qt5 and Qt6 and does\nthe same thing.\n\nOn Qt 5, QString::fromLocal8Bit() uses QTextCodec::codecForLocale(),\nwhereas on Qt 6 it is the same as QString::fromUtf8(), but Qt 6\nalways forces the process locale to use UTF-8 on UN*X anyway so it\ngives the same result:\nhttps://github.com/qt/qtbase/commit/419f42903154489e2dace8d1eba183036275448b\n\nThe other cases of QTextCodec are harder to eliminate; Qt drastically\nreduced the number of included codecs with the Qt6 alternative unless\nbuilding with ICU. The Qt Company's binary packages for Windows aren't\nbuilt with libicu, so that approach to preserving GUI support for\nShift-JIS, KOI8-R, Windows-1252 etc. would make development more\nchallenging.",
